  "stages": [
    {
      "id": "researcher_notes",
      "type": "Information",
      "label": {
        "en": "Researcher notes (delete before fielding)"
      },
      "title": {
        "en": "Notes for the research team"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "text",
          "type": "text",
          "content": {
            "en": "**About this draft.** Sketch drafted this protocol from a study description. Review every stage before fielding.\n\n**Study.** A messy study of support.\n\n**Changes Sketch made.**\n- Two node types / relationships use id \"person\"; the second became \"person_2\". Give each its own id.\n- Consent attribute \"participant_consent\" was replaced by the built-in consent question (includeConsent); the interview ends if the participant declines.\n- Two different attributes use id \"age\"; the second became \"age_2\" and every reference to \"age\" points at the first. Give each attribute its own id.\n- ordered attribute \"mood\" needs at least 2 options; it was turned into free text.\n- optionScores of \"scale\" must be one distinct whole number per option (3); they were dropped and options scored 1..n.\n- Stage \"early\" uses \"person\" nodes before any earlier nameGenerator creates them. The stage was removed.\n- Skip condition tests \"smokes\" on egoAttributes, which no EARLIER stage collects.\n- mode skip_if has no usable conditions; the stage is always shown.\n- Form attribute \"undefined_attr\" is not an attribute of egoAttributes. Matching attributes there: age (number), age_2 (text), smokes (yes_no), mood (text), scale (ordered).\n- Form attribute \"closeness\" is not an attribute of egoAttributes. Matching attributes there: age (number), age_2 (text), smokes (yes_no), mood (text), scale (ordered).\n- Prompt without text removed.\n- a yes_no value must be \"yes\" or \"no\" (got \"maybe\"). Condition removed.\n- Bin attribute \"close\" on node type \"person\" is yes_no, but this needs ordered or single_choice. Matching attributes there: person_closeness (ordered).\n- narrative \"story\" needs an EARLIER sociogram of node type \"person\" (it reuses that map's positions). Add one, or remove the narrative. The stage was removed.\n- relationship \"knows\" is not declared. Declared: person_2.\n- Highlight \"person_closeness\" is ordered; highlights must be yes_no. Prompt removed.\n- relationship \"person\" is not declared. Declared: person_2.\n- relationshipForm \"edge_form\" has no valid relationship. The stage was removed.\n- mode show_only_if has no usable conditions; the stage is always shown."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "welcome",
      "type": "Information",
      "label": {
        "en": "Welcome"
      },
      "title": {
        "en": "Welcome"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "text",
          "type": "text",
          "content": {
            "en": "Hi"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "consent",
      "type": "EgoForm",
      "label": {
        "en": "Consent"
      },
      "introductionPanel": {
        "title": {
          "en": "Taking part"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Do you consent?"
        }
      },
      "form": {
        "fields": [
          {
            "variable": "ego_consent",
            "prompt": {
              "en": "Do you agree to take part in this study?"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "about",
      "type": "EgoForm",
      "label": {
        "en": "About"
      },
      "introductionPanel": {
        "title": {
          "en": "About you"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Please answer the following questions about yourself."
        }
      },
      "form": {
        "fields": [
          {
            "variable": "ego_age",
            "prompt": {
              "en": "Age?"
            }
          },
          {
            "variable": "ego_smokes",
            "prompt": {
              "en": "Do you smoke?"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "skipLogic": {
        "action": "SKIP",
        "filter": {
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "rule_1",
              "type": "ego",
              "options": {
                "attribute": "ego_consent",
                "operator": "EXACTLY",
                "value": false
